= Network — Technical =

== Graph representation ==
A simple network can be represented as graph:

<pre>
G = (V, E)
</pre>

with vertices V and edges E.

Weighted networks add weights w_ij; directed networks distinguish i→j from j→i.

== Structural measures ==
Common measures include:

<pre>
degree k_i
shortest-path distance d(i,j)
clustering coefficient
centrality
community/modularity measures
spectral properties
connectivity/percolation thresholds
</pre>

== Beyond static simple graphs ==
Real networks can be temporal, multilayer, bipartite, hypergraphic, spatial, adaptive, uncertain, or dynamically coupled.

